WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.435
This is a healthy lower jaw.

00:00:02.785 --> 00:00:05.067
The bone comes up close to the necks of the teeth.

00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:10.475
Gum disease (periodontitis) slowly wears away the gum and bone that hold your teeth.

00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:12.660
Red shows the bone that has gone.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.215
Dentists use stages one to four. Stage one is the mildest.

00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:20.212
By stage four, much of the bone has gone.

00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:23.293
Teeth can become loose, move or need to come out.

00:00:24.093 --> 00:00:26.044
Lost bone mostly does not grow back,

00:00:26.044 --> 00:00:28.701
but you and your dentist can control the disease.

00:00:29.051 --> 00:00:31.355
See a dentist if your gums keep bleeding.
